NestJS modular monolith and headless React front end whose architecture is **executable**:
layer boundaries, authorization, transaction participation, the HTTP contract and the
migration journal are enforced by specs, lint and the type checker — not by convention or
code review.

## What the codebase guarantees

| Guarantee                       | How it is enforced                                                                                                                                                       |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Layer boundaries are real       | `module-boundaries.spec.ts` resolves every production import; across modules only `api/facades`, `api/events` and `*.module.ts` are legal targets                        |
| Authorization is fail-closed    | every route declares exactly one access mode; no declaration → authenticated, no policy provider → 403; `authz-coverage` fails an undeclared route                       |
| Transactions are declared       | `@Transactional` / `@ReadOnly` / `@NonTransactional("reason")` on every use case (`transactional-coverage`); the pool is private to the kernel, the executor lives in ALS |
| Events cannot be lost           | transactional outbox: publishing outside a transaction throws; at-least-once, backoff, dead-letter, per-aggregate FIFO, replay; direct `EventEmitter.emit` is forbidden |
| Mutations are idempotent        | `Idempotency-Key` store with request hash and response snapshot — same payload replays, different payload is rejected                                                   |
| Context is never a parameter    | `RequestContext` over AsyncLocalStorage carries correlation/causation, actor and tenant; every dispatcher opens one                                                      |
| The HTTP contract has one truth | Zod → DTOs → `openapi.json` → generated client (`@platform/api-client`); CI fails on an uncommitted contract; a change breaks on the front, never silently in the API    |
| Errors are a contract           | every error is RFC 7807 `application/problem+json` with `correlationId`, never a stack, SQL or path                                                                     |

Quality gates: TypeScript `strict` + `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` + `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`,
`any` and `eslint-disable` are errors; Vitest 4 as the single runner over four projects
(`api`, `api-int`, `api-e2e`, `web`) against real Postgres and Redis (testcontainers);
coverage floor of 90 % on every metric, never lowered; pre-push runs
`db:check:journal → typecheck → test:coverage`.

## Getting started

Supported dev platforms: macOS, Linux, WSL2 on Windows. Native Windows is not supported —
`scripts/sync-agent-skills.mjs` mirrors the agent skills via symlinks.

```
cp apps/api/.env.example apps/api/.env
docker compose up -d
pnpm install
pnpm --filter api db:migrate:run
pnpm dev
```

Front at `http://localhost:{% if web_stack == 'next' %}3001{% else %}5173{% endif %}`, API at `http://localhost:3000` (Scalar at `/docs`).

```
apps/api/      NestJS — kernel in src/shared, modules in src/modules
apps/web/      headless {% if web_stack == 'next' %}React/Next.js — transport, route access, access guard, unstyled layout{% else %}React/Vite — transport, router, access guard, unstyled layout{% endif %}
packages/      api-client (generated from openapi.json), eslint and tsconfig presets
docs/          handbooks, ADRs, advisories
.claude/ .agents/   agent harness (hooks, skills, agents); AGENTS.md is also CLAUDE.md
```

## Platform origin and updates

The kernel, the front-end shell, the harness and the handbooks come from
`platform-template` (version in `.copier-answers.yml` — never edit by hand). Platform
modules are installed on demand from a versioned catalog with
`pnpm platform module add <entry>`; fixes to installed entries arrive as advisories and
the platform itself updates with `copier update`. The rule that keeps updates
conflict-free: **this repository adds files; it does not edit platform files**.

